I revisited this today, and it seems like what is needed to trigger the buffer leak is to create a socket _and_ to send at least two messages on the socket, while either pinging or sending gptp messages to the board.
Meaning that this triggers a buffer leak for me:
```
[...]
void main(void) {
        [...]
        s = zsock_socket(AF_PACKET, SOCK_DGRAM, 0x22f0);
        [...]
        zsock_sendto(s, pdu, PDU_SIZE, 0, (struct sockaddr *)&addr, sizeof(addr));
        k_sleep(K_SECONDS(10));
        zsock_sendto(s, pdu, PDU_SIZE, 0, (struct sockaddr *)&addr, sizeof(addr));
        while(1){k_sleep(K_SECONDS(10));}
        return;
}
```
While this does not:
```
[...]
void main(void) {
        [...]
        s = zsock_socket(AF_PACKET, SOCK_DGRAM, 0x22f0);
        [...]
        zsock_sendto(s, pdu, PDU_SIZE, 0, (struct sockaddr *)&addr, sizeof(addr));
        while(1){k_sleep(K_SECONDS(10));}
        return;
}
```
After the second message is sent, the incoming messages fill up the rx buffer.
